+## 2026-06-10 (Operational retrospective — 2026.06.368)
+
+- Wrote `results/operational_retro_2026_06_368.json` (schema carnot.operational_retro.v64). The authoritative TIMING DATA block again reported **0 experiment commits since activation** and both RTX 3090s idle (0%). Per the GPU-idle rule this is NOT flagged — there are 0 compute-bound tasks in the block, so `gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null`, locked numerics stay 0/empty, and `estimated_time_savings_pct=0` (no real timing to optimize; no wall-time fabricated per the exp3984 INFRA-FIX spec).
+- **Headline finding — detector_gap_suspected=true, 5th consecutive false zero (.363/.365/.366/.367/.368).** The zero is a known milestone->commit detector artifact, NOT an empty milestone: ~10 .368 artifacts exist on disk and in this changelog (exp3975 GAP-4 build, exp3976 trm-rerank, exp3978 verifier-vs-judge efficiency win, exp3979 world-model-gen, exp3980 incremental-levels, exp3981 fourth-game, exp3982 ArcMemo solve-transfer, exp3983 hardware-continuity, exp3984 detector-fix, exp3985 capstone_v368; exp3977 genuinely absent = capstone "missing1").
+- **Meta-finding:** exp3984 landed `complete: retro_commit_detector_fixed_backfill_counts_restored` THIS SAME MILESTONE, yet this retro still received a zero timing block — so the fix is NOT verified end-to-end on the live retro-timing feed. Top-3 highest-leverage actions: (1) prove the exp3984 fix reaches the LIVE retro-timing generator via an end-to-end test over .368 (must report ~10, not 0); (2) wire the detector_gap_suspected self-check into the retro generator so zero-count-with-artifacts fails loud, never silent; (3) add a glob-based experiments_completed fallback (results/experiment_*.json since the activation SHA) as a detector-independent cross-check.
+- Appended the .368 narrative to `docs/research-log.md`. No edits to operator-curated docs (roadmap.md, index.html, README.md), research_conductor.py, or research-roadmap.yaml.
